Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: mark the periodic airtime and SCS commands as reads

The core starts a full reset through mt7915_mcu_cmd_lost() for a command
without MT76_MCU_CMD_READ that an L1 SER refuses with -ESHUTDOWN or whose
answer it cuts off. mt76 marks its own periodic queries as reads, so that
they do not turn an L1 SER into a full reset.

mt7915_mac_work() asks for the per-station airtime with GET_ALL_STA_STATS
every 500 ms, and scs_work sends the SCS statistics every second while
WED RX is active. Both run until mt7915_mac_reset_work() cancels them,
after the interrupt path has set MT76_MCU_RESET. The airtime command only
reads: the answer comes as an event, and the counters are cleared through
the WTBL. scs_work sends new statistics a second later. Mark both as reads.
---
--- a/mt7915/mcu.c
+++ b/mt7915/mcu.c
@@ -6027,8 +6027,11 @@ int mt7915_mcu_set_scs_stats(struct mt79
 	if (phy->scs_ctrl.tx_bytes_last_sec < phy->scs_ctrl.rx_bytes_last_sec / 9)
 		req.rx_only_mode = true;
 
-	return mt76_mcu_send_msg(&dev->mt76, MCU_EXT_CMD(SCS_FEATURE_CTRL),
-				 &req, sizeof(req), NULL);
+	/* scs_work sends these statistics again each second, so a lost one
+	 * leaves no firmware state to restore
+	 */
+	return mt76_mcu_send_msg(&dev->mt76, MCU_EXT_CMD(SCS_FEATURE_CTRL) |
+				 MT76_MCU_CMD_READ, &req, sizeof(req), NULL);
 }
 
 void mt7915_mcu_scs_sta_poll(struct work_struct *work)
@@ -6087,6 +6090,6 @@ int mt7915_mcu_get_all_sta_info(struct m
 		.tag = tag,
 	};
 
-	return mt76_mcu_send_msg(dev, MCU_EXT_CMD(GET_ALL_STA_STATS),
-				&req, sizeof(req), false);
+	return mt76_mcu_send_msg(dev, MCU_EXT_CMD(GET_ALL_STA_STATS) |
+				 MT76_MCU_CMD_READ, &req, sizeof(req), false);
 }
